{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{# Card search syntax: the keys of SearchController::$searchKeys #}
{% block body %}
  <div class="main white container" id="syntax">
    {% include 'alerts.html.twig' %}
    <div class="page-header"><h1>{{ 'nav.syntax' | trans }}</h1></div>
    <ul>
      <li>A search is one or more <b>conditions</b> separated by spaces; a card must meet all of them:
        <code>f:elven t:companion</code></li>
      <li>A condition without a key searches card names and subtitles: <code>legolas</code>. A blueprint ID finds that card: <code>1_50</code></li>
      <li><code>|</code> means "or" within a condition: <code>f:elven|dwarven</code></li>
      <li>Quote values with spaces: <code>x:"spot an elf"</code></li>
      <li>Operators: <code>:</code> equals (or contains, for text), <code>!</code> is not, <code>&lt;</code> and <code>&gt;</code> for numbers</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <h3>Keys</h3>
        <table class="table table-condensed">
          <tr><td><code>x</code></td><td>game text</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>a</code></td><td>lore (flavor text)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>f</code></td><td>culture: <code>elven</code>, <code>dwarven</code>, <code>gandalf</code>, <code>gondor</code>, <code>rohan</code>, <code>shire</code>, <code>gollum</code>, <code>dunland</code>, <code>isengard</code>, <code>men</code>, <code>moria</code>, <code>orc</code>, <code>raider</code>, <code>ringwraith</code>, <code>sauron</code>, <code>uruk_hai</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>d</code></td><td>side: <code>free_peoples</code> or <code>shadow</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>t</code></td><td>card type: <code>companion</code>, <code>ally</code>, <code>minion</code>, <code>possession</code>, <code>artifact</code>, <code>condition</code>, <code>event</code>, <code>follower</code>, <code>site</code>, <code>the_one_ring</code>, <code>map</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>k</code></td><td>subtype: race, item class or phase (<code>k:elf</code>, <code>k:hand weapon</code>, <code>k:skirmish</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>o</code></td><td>twilight cost</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>s</code></td><td>strength</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>v</code></td><td>vitality</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>z</code></td><td>resistance</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>n</code></td><td>site number (home site for allies)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>h</code></td><td>shadow number of a site</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>g</code></td><td>signet: <code>frodo</code>, <code>aragorn</code>, <code>gandalf</code>, <code>theoden</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>u</code></td><td>unique: <code>u:1</code> or <code>u:0</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>e</code></td><td>set number: <code>e:1</code>, <code>e:101</code> (V1)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>c</code></td><td>block, by number: 1 Promotional, 2 Fellowship, 3 Towers, 4 King, 5 War of the Ring, 6 Hunters, 7 Players Council</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>r</code></td><td>rarity: <code>C</code>, <code>U</code>, <code>R</code>, <code>R+</code>, <code>P</code>, <code>S</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>i</code></td><td><code>i:errata</code> for Players Council errata blueprints (hidden otherwise)</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <h3>Examples</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><code>f:elven t:companion</code> &ndash; Elven companions</li>
          <li><code>d:shadow o&lt;2 t:minion</code> &ndash; Shadow minions costing 0 or 1</li>
          <li><code>x:archery f!elven</code> &ndash; non-Elven cards that mention archery</li>
          <li><code>t:site n:4 c:2</code> &ndash; site 4 in the Fellowship block</li>
          <li><code>k:ranger s&gt;6</code> &ndash; Rangers with strength 7 or more</li>
          <li><code>i:errata f:gondor</code> &ndash; Gondor PC errata</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Card culture symbols in game text are written <code>[ELVEN]</code>, <code>[SAURON]</code> and so on.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
